WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:19.416
Ten passed, and we were still living in the place we called New Switzerland.

2
00:00:20.957 --> 00:00:24.679
We built a watch tower on an island in the bay and added two cannons.

3
00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:27.481
We made many improvements at Rockburg.

4
00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:31.643
The swamp, cleared and drained, was now a large lake.

5
00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:36.725
Beneath the trees, old Hurry, the ostrich, walked at a dignified pace.

6
00:00:37.745 --> 00:00:39.786
My boys retained their love of animals.

7
00:00:40.626 --> 00:00:45.087
They now had a beautiful white cow, a bull, and two new donkeys.

8
00:00:45.927 --> 00:00:47.988
Jack had a descendant of Fangs the jackal.

9
00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:49.348
He named it Coco.

10
00:00:50.168 --> 00:00:52.249
The boys were fine, handsome fellows.

11
00:00:53.169 --> 00:00:56.950
Fritz, now 25, was very strong and high-spirited.

12
00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.851
Ernest, 23, was still calm and studious.

13
00:01:01.852 --> 00:01:05.905
Jack, 21, was known for his agility and sense of humor.

14
00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:09.906
And Franz, 18, was a lively youth.

15
00:01:10.926 --> 00:01:14.087
My older sons often went away on expeditions by themselves.

16
00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.528
One evening I realized Fritz had been away all day.

17
00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:22.430
Anxious to see him return, I went to our watch tower with Ernest and Jack.

18
00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:26.591
When we finally spotted Fritz's kayak, it was moving very slowly.

19
00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:29.191
"Welcome back from wherever you've been!"

20
00:01:29.572 --> 00:01:30.652
I cried when he landed.

21
00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.286
"You seem to have a lot of cargo there."

22
00:01:33.306 --> 00:01:38.590
"Yes, and my trip has led to discoveries that will tempt us to go out again," he replied.

23
00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:41.513
Ernest and Jack helped Fritz unload the kayak.

24
00:01:42.293 --> 00:01:44.595
After supper Fritz told us of his adventures.

25
00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:48.599
"I paddled for a long time until I came to another bay," he said.

26
00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:51.281
"The water was as clear as crystal.

27
00:01:51.982 --> 00:01:53.323
I could see beds of oysters.

28
00:01:54.184 --> 00:01:57.627
I brought up several clusters and left them on the beach while I went back for more.

29
00:01:58.347 --> 00:02:02.090
When I returned, the shells had opened a bit, and I think I found some pearls."

30
00:02:03.051 --> 00:02:04.472
He held out his hand to show us.

31
00:02:04.492 --> 00:02:07.034
"Those are pearls indeed!"

32
00:02:07.135 --> 00:02:07.455
I said.

33
00:02:07.475 --> 00:02:11.318
"And they may prove a source of wealth if we are ever rescued."

34
00:02:12.179 --> 00:02:17.243
"After I gathered my oysters," Fritz continued, "I crossed Pearl Bay, as I named it.

35
00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.845
There I saw thousands of seabirds.

36
00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.887
They must have thought I was invading their territory.

37
00:02:23.588 --> 00:02:25.470
The next thing I knew, they were attacking me."

38
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:26.991
"What did you do?"

39
00:02:27.411 --> 00:02:28.052
asked my wife.

40
00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:32.209
"I waved my paddle over my head and managed to hit an albatross!

41
00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:35.310
It fell into the water, and the other birds flew away.

42
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.691
And then—well, I guess that's the end of my story."

43
00:02:40.491 --> 00:02:43.892
The next morning Fritz drew me aside because he had more to tell me.

44
00:02:43.912 --> 00:02:47.933
"There was something extraordinary about that albatross," he said.

45
00:02:47.953 --> 00:02:51.914
"I lifted it onto my kayak and found a rag around one leg.

46
00:02:52.594 --> 00:02:55.815
When I removed the rag, I was amazed to see words written on it."

47
00:02:55.835 --> 00:02:57.396
"What did they say?"

48
00:02:57.676 --> 00:02:58.096
I asked.

49
00:02:59.088 --> 00:03:01.989
"'Save an unfortunate Englishwoman from the smoking rock.'"

50
00:03:02.009 --> 00:03:04.490
"What!" I cried in astonishment.

51
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.931
"Another human being is here in this lonely place?"

52
00:03:06.951 --> 00:03:10.753
"The bird was beginning to show signs of life," Fritz continued.

53
00:03:10.773 --> 00:03:13.154
"So I had to decide what to do.

54
00:03:13.874 --> 00:03:17.095
I quickly tore a strip from my handkerchief and wrote, 'Do not despair!

55
00:03:17.315 --> 00:03:17.936
Help is near!'"

56
00:03:18.636 --> 00:03:21.377
Fritz carefully tied his message around one of the bird's legs.

57
00:03:22.137 --> 00:03:24.278
Then he devoted himself to reviving the bird.

58
00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:28.460
After drinking some water, it suddenly took off and headed west.

59
00:03:29.236 --> 00:03:30.777
"I lost sight of it," said Fritz.

60
00:03:30.797 --> 00:03:34.741
"But I keep wondering: Will my note ever reach this Englishwoman?

61
00:03:35.421 --> 00:03:37.643
Will I be able to find her and save her?"

62
00:03:37.663 --> 00:03:41.666
"You were wise to keep this part of your story from the others," I said.

63
00:03:41.686 --> 00:03:44.529
"Until we know more, we must not excite them.

64
00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:47.871
It's possible that those words were written long ago.

65
00:03:48.732 --> 00:03:50.914
By now the unhappy woman may have died.

66
00:03:51.654 --> 00:03:55.237
The 'smoking rock' must be a volcano, and there are none here."

67
00:03:56.078 --> 00:03:58.460
Fritz, however, refused to be discouraged.

68
00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:01.570
It was obvious he hoped that he could rescue this woman.

69
00:04:02.371 --> 00:04:04.832
In fact, I was just as excited as he was.

70
00:04:05.773 --> 00:04:08.035
But I felt it wise to contain my excitement.

71
00:04:08.835 --> 00:04:12.698
After some discussion we decided that Fritz should go in search of the Englishwoman.

72
00:04:13.439 --> 00:04:16.101
He would need to modify his kayak to carry two people.

73
00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:20.164
And he would need enough food in case he was away for a long time.

74
00:04:21.005 --> 00:04:25.088
Impatient as he was to leave, Fritz knew he must take some time to prepare.

75
00:04:25.952 --> 00:04:29.814
We returned to the house and saw the other boys busily opening oysters.

76
00:04:30.695 --> 00:04:31.796
They were very excited.

77
00:04:31.816 --> 00:04:33.356
"Look, Father!"

78
00:04:33.697 --> 00:04:34.297
said Franz.

79
00:04:34.317 --> 00:04:35.798
"I found a pearl!"

80
00:04:35.818 --> 00:04:38.700
"Let's establish a pearl fishery at once!"

81
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:39.680
said Jack.

82
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:45.864
"If we built a hut at Pearl Bay, we could harvest oysters on a regular basis," Ernest pointed

83
00:04:45.964 --> 00:04:49.226
out. "Let's take the sailboat to Pearl Bay," I said.

84
00:04:50.046 --> 00:04:55.314
Fritz winked at me and then remarked in an innocent tone, "I've been thinking of adding another seat

85
00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:57.540
to the kayak in case someone ever needs a ride."
